# Git versioning

- Relevant work belongs in Git; no parallel shadow copies of project results.
- **Commits / push / PRs only when the user explicitly asks.**
- Before commit: `git status`, `git diff`, `git log -5` in parallel; message via HEREDOC; focus on why.
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, keys, credentials).
- Do not change `git config`. No force-push to main/master, no hard reset, no `--no-verify` unless explicitly requested.
- Amend only when the user asked or a hook auto-fixed files, HEAD is yours, and not yet pushed.
